{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update-32.json\",\"summary\":\"Closing the recovery scenario's explicit limitation that no snapshot was installed. The successor adds a second test to the same harness: after a payload is committed on all nodes, node 2 is stopped, a second payload is committed by the remaining nodes, and the leader then takes a snapshot at its last index with the storage's ConfState and compacts its log to that index, so the stopped member's missing entries are gone from the append path and resynchronization must happen through snapshot installation. Node 2 is rebuilt from its own storage, the clock is advanced fifteen rounds with delivery between rounds so the leader contacts it and sends the snapshot, and three comparisons cover snapshot installation, a fresh proposal returning, and that proposal being applied by the resynchronized member. A local run shows the intended sequence: the snapshot is created at index 3 with term 1 and the log compacted to 3, node 2 installs it with applied and commit index 3 while reporting leader 1, and the later proposal returns with no error and is applied by node 2 with the payload observed on all three nodes. The submission is validated with execution requested; it tests the resynchronization mechanism that the append-path recovery scenario left out, and its receipt will be interpreted next.\"}"}}
